
*** Functional requirements ***

> User should be able to input a start location, destination and get estimated fare
> User should be able to request a ride based on estimate 
> Drivers should be able to accept/deny request and navigate to pickup/dropoff

Out of scope : ratings/scheduling a ride etc 

*** Non-functional requirements ***
> Low latency matching (< 1 min or failure)
> In terms of CAP , we care about consistency of matching (their should be 1-1 on ride and driver), it should be highly available
outside of this 
> Handle high theroughput (peak/special event) {100s of thousands of requests in a region}

Out of scope : GDPR/user privacy/ fault tolerance/monitoring/metrics/alerting 

Estimates will do later in HLDs when they directly impact our design

*** Core Entity ***

Ride 
Driver
Rider
Location Entity (has location of all drivers to quickly match them based on proximity)

*** API ***

For the first requiremnet , it looks like a GET but we need to get sensitive info like location etc that if taken as query string makes it messy 

POST /ride/fare-estimate --> Partial<Ride>

{
    source,destination
}

And this info will be peristsed in a db etc because this would be used later to request ride potentially. Ex rideId will be needed in next request

PUT /ride/request --> 200 (since this is async) (can be patch also)

{
    rideId
}

For actual matching we will need drivers location 

POST /location/update 

{
    longitude,latitude
}

Now for drivers to accept or deny 

PATCH /ride/driver/accept

{
    rideId, true/false
}

We need one endpoint for navigation

PATCH /ride/driver/update --> lat/long they need to go

{
    rideId, status : {PICKED_UP, DROPPED_OFF}
}

We don't put userId in any of the request (example who pickedup ride), these will be put in headers since body is securityRisk


